<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Miguel Juárez Celman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1844–1909</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Miguel Juárez Celman was an Argentine politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-autonomist-party">National Autonomist Party</a> and president from 1886 to 1890. His government encouraged heavy foreign borrowing and speculation, which ended in the financial crisis of 1890. After the armed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolution-of-the-park">Revolution of the Park</a> in July 1890 he lost the support of his party and resigned in August.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/miguel-juarez-celman.jpg" alt="Miguel Juárez Celman" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juarez_celman_president.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
